{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Elohim you shall not curse.</b> These are the judges, and they are the priests, the Levites, with whom the Torah is." "<b>And a leader among your people you shall not curse.</b> In secret or in public. And the Gaon [Saadia] distinguished between קללה and מארה. And this leader is the king, mentioned in Mishneh Torah. And when we examined the verses that follow one after another, down to \"and in all that I have said to you you shall keep\" (below 23:13), we found most of them concern the poor, as though they are joined to the passage of \"if you lend money.\" Yefet said a reason for mentioning \"Elohim you shall not curse\": perhaps the poor person, in the abundance of his distress at night, if the lender passes by and does not return his pledge to him, he will curse the judge who ruled that he may take his pledge."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:27.397055853Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}